  systematic, not a one-off -- the same coordinate is off in every committed run:
    bb_bond     4 run(s), +3% to +15%
    intra_cn    7 run(s), +2% to +222%
    intra_pc   12 run(s), +220% to +418%
    The run's moments (sum / sumsq) are not written to the round npz, so the
    histogram is the only route to its sigma; for this coordinate the two
    disagree by 2-4x. Either the moments behind the recorded J came from a
    different sample set than the histogram, or the histogram is not the one
    that was scored. `results/pooled_sim_*.npz` DO carry sum/sumsq/n -- a round
    npz written with the same three keys per coordinate would settle it here.
    sharpest clue, ibi_chainA_r1, intra_pc: the histogram's own sigma is 0.03989, and
    the recorded sim/ref times the stored sigma is 0.01171. Same run, same
    file, two numbers for one quantity -- so it is a definition that changed
    between the two writes, not floating point.

